{"version": 2, "width": 100, "height": 30, "timestamp": 1778683025, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/bash", "TERM": "xterm-color"}, "title": "craftcargo: Rust → Ubuntu Packaging Made Easy"}
[0.010755, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[2J"]
[0.011306, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[0;36m═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[0;37m        craftcargo: Rust → Ubuntu Packaging Made Easy\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[0;36m═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[0;90mThis demo shows how craftcargo generates a complete debcraft.yaml\r\nfrom a Rust crate, ready for Ubuntu package building.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.013227, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m# Step 1: Let's see what craftcargo can do\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.015725, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[1mdebcargo --help\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.02364, "o", "Package Rust crates for Debian.\r\n\r\n\u001b[32mUsage:\u001b[0m \u001b[32mdebcargo\u001b[0m \u001b[32m<COMMAND>\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[33mCommands:\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[32mupdate\u001b[0m               Update the user's default crates.io index, outside of a workspace\r\n  \u001b[32mdeb-src-name\u001b[0m         Print the Debian package name for a crate\r\n  \u001b[32mextract\u001b[0m              Extract only a crate, without any other transformations\r\n  \u001b[32mpackage\u001b[0m              Package a Rust crate for Debian\r\n  \u001b[32mpackage-debcraft\u001b[0m     Package a Rust crate for debcraft (generates debcraft.yaml)\r\n  \u001b[32mbuild-order\u001b[0m          Print the transitive dependencies of a package in topological order\r\n  \u001b[32mdeb-dependencies\u001b[0m     Print the dependencies of a package in d/control format\r\n  \u001b[32mupdate-dependencies\u001b[0m  Update debian/control Build-Depends from workspace Cargo.toml files\r\n  \u001b[32mhelp\u001b[0m                 Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\r\n\r\n\u001b[33mOptions:\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[32m-h\u001b[0m, \u001b[32m--help\u001b[0m     Print help\r\n  \u001b[32m-V\u001b[0m, \u001b[32m--version\u001b[0m  Print version\r\n"]
[0.029938, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m# Step 2: Let's package 'tokio-util' — it has features, multiple deps, and licence complexity\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.032464, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m# First, what would the Debian source package be called?\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.034918, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[1mdebcargo deb-src-name tokio-util\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.197726, "o", "tokio-util\r\n"]
[0.206116, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m# Step 3: Generate the debcraft.yaml\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.208167, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[1mdebcargo package-debcraft tokio-util --directory ./output/tokio-util\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.223196, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[92m    Updating\u001b[0m crates.io index\r\n"]
[0.333588, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m# Step 4: Let's look at what was generated\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.335982, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[1mls -la ./output/tokio-util/\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.341935, "o", "total 80\r\ndrwxrwxr-x 1 lengau lengau   224 May 13 16:37 .\r\ndrwx------ 1 lengau lengau    20 May 13 16:37 ..\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 lengau lengau   104 Jan  1  1970 .cargo_vcs_info.json\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 lengau lengau 19268 Jul 24  2006 CHANGELOG.md\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 lengau lengau 23556 Jan  1  1970 Cargo.lock\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 lengau lengau  4883 Jan  1  1970 Cargo.toml\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 lengau lengau  2242 Jul 24  2006 Cargo.toml.orig\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 lengau lengau  1070 Jul 24  2006 LICENSE\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 lengau lengau   320 Jul 24  2006 README.md\r\ndrwxrwxr-x 1 lengau lengau  1098 May 13 16:37 debcraft\r\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 lengau lengau 10053 May 13 16:37 debcraft.yaml\r\ndrwxrwxr-x 1 lengau lengau   202 May 13 16:37 src\r\ndrwxrwxr-x 1 lengau lengau   804 May 13 16:37 tests\r\n"]
[0.347138, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m# Here's the debcraft.yaml:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.349682, "o", "\u001b[0;32mcraftcargo-demo \u001b[0;36m$ \u001b[0m\u001b[1mcat ./output/tokio-util/debcraft.yaml\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.353609, "o", "name: rust-tokio-util\r\nversion: 0.7.18-1\r\nsummary: Additional utilities for working with Tokio - Rust source code\r\nmaintainer: Debian Rust Maintainers <pkg-rust-maintainers@alioth-lists.debian.net>\r\nsection: rust\r\ncontact: Debian Rust Maintainers <pkg-rust-maintainers@alioth-lists.debian.net>\r\nsource-code: https://tokio.rs\r\nvcs-git: https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio\r\nlicense: MIT\r\nissues: https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/issues\r\ncustom-source-fields:\r\n  X-Cargo-Crate: tokio-util\r\n  X-Cargo-Crate-Version: 0.7.18\r\nparts:\r\n  check:\r\n    plugin: cargo\r\n    source: .\r\n    build-packages-arch:\r\n    - cargo:native\r\n    - rustc:native (>= 1.71)\r\n    - libstd-rust-dev\r\n    - package: librust-bytes-1+default-dev (>= 1.5.0)\r\n      profiles:\r\n      - nocheck\r\n    - package: librust-futures-core-0.3+default-dev\r\n      profiles:\r\n      - nocheck\r\n    - package: librust-futures-sink-0.3+default-dev\r\n      profiles:\r\n      - nocheck\r\n    - package: librust-pin-project-lite-0.2+default-dev (>= 0.2.11)\r\n      profiles:\r\n      - nocheck\r\n    - package: librust-tokio-1+default-dev (>= 1.44.0)\r\n      profiles:\r\n      - nocheck\r\n    - package: librust-tokio-1+sync-dev (>= 1.44.0)\r\n      profiles:\r\n      - nocheck\r\n    after:\r\n    - crate\r\n  crate:\r\n    plugin: dump\r\n    source: .\r\npackages:\r\n  librust-tokio-util+full-dev:\r\n    architectures: any\r\n    summary: Additional utilities for working with Tokio - feature \"full\"\r\n    description: This metapackage enables feature \"full\" for the Rust tokio-util crate, by pulling in any additional dependencies needed by that feature.\r\n    depends:\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util+codec-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util+compat-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util+io-util-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util+time-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util+net-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util+rt-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util+join-map-dev\r\n    provides:\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-0+full-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-0.7+full-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-0.7.18+full-dev\r\n    breaks:\r\n    - rustc (<< 1.71~)\r\n    multi-arch: same\r\n  librust-tokio-util+futures-io-dev:\r\n    architectures: any\r\n    summary: Additional utilities for working with Tokio - feature \"futures-io\" and 1 more\r\n    description: |-\r\n      This metapackage enables feature \"futures-io\" for the Rust tokio-util crate, by pulling in any additional dependencies needed by that feature.\r\n\r\n      Additionally, this package also provides the \"compat\" feature.\r\n    depends:\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-dev\r\n    - librust-futures-io-0.3+default-dev\r\n    provides:\r\n    - librust-tokio-util+compat-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-0+futures-io-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-0+compat-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-0.7+futures-io-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-0.7+compat-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-0.7.18+futures-io-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-0.7.18+compat-dev\r\n    breaks:\r\n    - rustc (<< 1.71~)\r\n    multi-arch: same\r\n  librust-tokio-util+futures-util-dev:\r\n    architectures: any\r\n    summary: Additional utilities for working with Tokio - feature \"futures-util\" and 1 more\r\n    description: |-\r\n      This metapackage enables feature \"futures-util\" for the Rust tokio-util crate, by pulling in any additional dependencies needed by that feature.\r\n\r\n      Additionally, this package also provides the \"__docs_rs\" feature.\r\n    depends:\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-dev\r\n    - librust-futures-util-0.3+default-dev\r\n    provides:\r\n    - librust-tokio-util+--docs-rs-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-0+futures-util-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-0+--docs-rs-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-0.7+futures-util-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-0.7+--docs-rs-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-0.7.18+futures-util-dev\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-0.7.18+--docs-rs-dev\r\n    breaks:\r\n    - rustc (<< 1.71~)\r\n    multi-arch: same\r\n  librust-tokio-util+hashbrown-dev:\r\n    architectures: any\r\n    summary: Additional utilities for working with Tokio - feature \"hashbrown\"\r\n    description: This metapackage enables feature \"hashbrown\" for the Rust tokio-util crate, by pulling in any additional dependencies needed by that feature.\r\n    depends:\r\n    - librust-tokio-util-dev\r\n    - librust-hashbrown-0.15-dev\r\n    provides:\r\n    - librust-"]
